From: EglantinePS5
Subject: [PATCH] up: EDEN_UP_SHADER_SET_PACK=1, the shader set file stores each program's code packed (about 900 MB to about 375 MB)

Switch: EDEN_UP_SHADER_SET_PACK (exact "1", read once; off by default).

Why: in the first console run of the before-play pass (13 Nov, run1382, T162) the shader list
(prep_shader_set.bin) was ready 708 s after the pass began. The log puts the time here: the records
were converted and written by 71 s ("dropped ..." lines, "31.8 s in all"), then nothing until
"62344 facts and 40972 programs stored once, 922 MB in all" at 738 s. Between those two lines the
code does only one thing: it writes the facts (about 18 MB) and each used program's lowered code
(about 780 MB) through AtomicFile's 8 MiB pieces. So 667 s went into writing about 800 MB, about
1.2 MB a second. The same code wrote the same part (860 MB file) in 75 s in test d4 (T138) and in
175 s in t110-s; why this run's disk was ten times slower is not checked (the records part of the
same run went at 10 MB a second or more; nothing else is logged in those 667 s). Lowering is not
the cost: all 41,169 programs were lowered in 3.3 s (55.7 s to 59.1 s).

What: with the switch, each program's code in the programs section is one zstd frame (level 1)
and the file's magic at both ends is "edenset4" (same layout otherwise). Measured on the d4 file
(763 MB of program code, 36,542 programs): 236 MB frame by frame, 2.4 s on the Mac (one thread).
The file shrinks from about 900 MB to about 375 MB (records 121 MB and facts 18 MB stay). Each
program's code is given back to memory as soon as it is written (about 800 MB held until the end
before). ReadRecords and ForEachProgramCode read both kinds; a damaged frame ends the read as a cut
file does. The stamp gets "programs packed 1", so turning the switch on or off makes the file
again once. An older build reads a packed file as another layout (nothing read) and its stamp
differs, so it converts again.

Expected time for the save before play: 375 MB instead of 900 MB, so about 30 s at d4's rate and
about 4-5 minutes at run1382's rate, plus about 5-8 s of packing on the console (not measured
there). Reading: each record's programs are unpacked when the record is read (about 6 GB of
unpacking for a whole pass of 119,524 records; zstd unpacks at 1 GB a second or more), small
next to the pipeline builds.

Off: one cached switch read per conversion and per file read (the magic check); the file and the
stamp are as before. shader_set.cpp is not among the translation id's files
(tools/gen-translation-id.py), so this patch alone does not move the id. Not checked: a run, a
build.
---
diff --git a/src/video_core/shader_set.cpp b/src/video_core/shader_set.cpp
index 780b73d8dc..4704cf2c66 100644
--- a/src/video_core/shader_set.cpp
+++ b/src/video_core/shader_set.cpp
@@ -132,6 +132,19 @@ size_t NupCacheCapMiB() {
     return mib == 0 ? 512 : std::max<size_t>(static_cast<size_t>(mib), 16);
 }
 
+/// EDEN_UP_SHADER_SET_PACK=1 (0830; exact "1", read once; off by default): each program's lowered
+/// code in the programs section is one zstd frame (level 1), and the file says so with the magic
+/// "edenset4" at both ends; records and facts are as before. Why: on 13 Nov (run1382, T162) the
+/// facts and programs (about 800 MB, almost all lowered code) took 667 s to write before play, at
+/// about 1.2 MB a second; the same 780 MB had taken 75 s in test d4. The code shrinks about 3.2
+/// times (763 MB to 236 MB measured on d4's file, frame by frame), so the file goes from about
+/// 900 MB to about 375 MB. A file of either kind is read by ReadRecords and ForEachProgramCode;
+/// an older build reads a packed file as one of another layout (empty), and its stamp differs.
+bool PackAsked() {
+    static const bool asked = Common::PeSwitch("EDEN_UP_SHADER_SET_PACK");
+    return asked;
+}
+
 /// Written whole under a temporary name, committed to disk, then renamed over the final name:
 /// a kill at any moment leaves the final name as it was (absent, or the last complete file).
 class AtomicFile {
@@ -202,6 +215,7 @@ std::string ExtractorLines() {
     // 0780: a set with compute records is another file (off: no line, the stamp as before).
     if (ComputeAsked()) lines += "compute 1\n";
     if (MeshAsked()) lines += "mesh 1\n"; // 0782
+    if (PackAsked()) lines += "programs packed 1\n"; // 0830 (off: no line, the stamp as before)
     // EDEN_UP_SHADER_SET_RECONVERT=<n> (a test aid): a number in the stamp, so a set made with
     // another number (or none) is converted again once, e.g. to time the conversion.
     if (const size_t again = SwitchNumber("EDEN_UP_SHADER_SET_RECONVERT", 0); again != 0) {
@@ -444,6 +458,29 @@ void AppendEnvironment(std::vector<char>& out, std::span<const char> fact,
 }
 
 constexpr char SetMagic[9] = "edenset3";
+constexpr char PackedMagic[9] = "edenset4"; // 0830: the same layout, each program's code packed
+/// 0830: the largest lowered program a packed file may unpack to (MaximumInstructions native
+/// instructions make well under 4 MiB of lowered code).
+constexpr u64 MaxPackedProgramBytes = u64{16} << 20;
+
+/// 0830: unpacks one program's stored bytes (one zstd frame) into `code`; false when damaged.
+bool UnpackProgram(ZSTD_DCtx* context, std::span<const char> stored, std::vector<char>& code) {
+    const unsigned long long size = ZSTD_getFrameContentSize(stored.data(), stored.size());
+    if (size == ZSTD_CONTENTSIZE_ERROR || size == ZSTD_CONTENTSIZE_UNKNOWN ||
+        size > MaxPackedProgramBytes) {
+        return false;
+    }
+    code.resize(static_cast<size_t>(size));
+    const size_t made = ZSTD_decompressDCtx(context, code.data(), code.size(), stored.data(),
+                                            stored.size());
+    return !ZSTD_isError(made) && made == code.size();
+}
+struct FreeDContext {
+    void operator()(ZSTD_DCtx* context) const { ZSTD_freeDCtx(context); }
+};
+struct FreeCContext {
+    void operator()(ZSTD_CCtx* context) const { ZSTD_freeCCtx(context); }
+};
 /// sizeof(ComputePipelineCacheKey): a record with a key this long is a compute record (0780);
 /// a graphics key is 1,056 bytes.
 constexpr u32 ComputeKeyBytes = 24;
@@ -804,7 +841,10 @@ Outputs Prepare(u64 title, const std::filesystem::path& title_dir,
         // key), then each used fact once, then each used program's lowered code once, then where
         // those three parts are. Layout 1 wrote every record's environments whole: 4.3 GB for
         // Ocarina's 113,054 records, and the PS5 writes that file at 1-1.5 MB a second.
-        file.Write(Bytes{reinterpret_cast<const u8*>(SetMagic), 8});
+        // 0830: a packed file's magic says so at both ends.
+        const bool pack = PackAsked();
+        const char* const magic = pack ? PackedMagic : SetMagic;
+        file.Write(Bytes{reinterpret_cast<const u8*>(magic), 8});
         file.Write(PipelineCacheVersion);
         std::map<std::string, size_t> dropped;
         std::vector<u64> used_programs; // lowered hashes with at least one converted record
@@ -944,20 +984,41 @@ Outputs Prepare(u64 title, const std::filesystem::path& title_dir,
             ++fact_count;
         }
         const u64 programs_at = file.Written();
+        // 0830: packed, each program's code is one zstd frame (level 1) and its memory is given
+        // back once written (nothing reads the lowered code after this loop).
+        std::unique_ptr<ZSTD_CCtx, FreeCContext> packer{pack ? ZSTD_createCCtx() : nullptr};
+        if (pack && !packer) throw std::runtime_error("no zstd context");
+        std::vector<u8> packed;
+        u64 code_bytes = 0;
         for (u32 index = 0; index < r.programs.size(); ++index) {
             if (!used_program[index]) continue;
-            const auto& code = lowered[index]->code;
+            auto& code = lowered[index]->code;
             file.Write(index);
             file.Write(lowered[index]->hash);
-            file.Write(static_cast<u64>(code.size() * 8));
-            file.Write(Bytes{reinterpret_cast<const u8*>(code.data()), code.size() * 8});
+            code_bytes += code.size() * 8;
+            if (pack) {
+                packed.resize(ZSTD_compressBound(code.size() * 8));
+                const size_t size = ZSTD_compressCCtx(packer.get(), packed.data(), packed.size(),
+                                                      code.data(), code.size() * 8, 1);
+                if (ZSTD_isError(size)) throw std::runtime_error("program packing failed");
+                file.Write(static_cast<u64>(size));
+                file.Write(Bytes{packed.data(), size});
+                std::vector<u64>{}.swap(code);
+            } else {
+                file.Write(static_cast<u64>(code.size() * 8));
+                file.Write(Bytes{reinterpret_cast<const u8*>(code.data()), code.size() * 8});
+            }
             ++program_count;
         }
+        if (pack) {
+            LOG_INFO(Render_Vulkan, "Shader set: EDEN_UP_SHADER_SET_PACK=1: {} MB of program code "
+                     "stored as {} MB", code_bytes >> 20, (file.Written() - programs_at) >> 20);
+        }
         for (const u64 value : {u64{12}, u64{converted}, facts_at, fact_count, programs_at,
                                 program_count}) {
             file.Write(value);
         }
-        file.Write(Bytes{reinterpret_cast<const u8*>(SetMagic), 8});
+        file.Write(Bytes{reinterpret_cast<const u8*>(magic), 8});
         LOG_INFO(Render_Vulkan, "Shader set: {} facts and {} programs stored once, {} MB in all; "
                  "{:.1f} s", fact_count, program_count, file.Written() >> 20, seconds());
         // The old stamp goes first (it must never sit beside the new files), then records, then
@@ -1055,9 +1116,13 @@ bool ReadRecords(
         seek(0);
         file.read(magic.data(), magic.size());
         get(version);
-        if (std::memcmp(magic.data(), SetMagic, 8) != 0 || version != cache_version) {
+        // 0830: "edenset4" is the same layout with each program's code packed.
+        const bool packed = std::memcmp(magic.data(), PackedMagic, 8) == 0;
+        if ((!packed && std::memcmp(magic.data(), SetMagic, 8) != 0) || version != cache_version) {
             return true; // another layout's or another version's file: nothing to read
         }
+        std::unique_ptr<ZSTD_DCtx, FreeDContext> unpacker{packed ? ZSTD_createDCtx() : nullptr};
+        if (packed && !unpacker) return false;
         std::error_code ec;
         const std::string identity = fmt::format(
             "{} {} {}", path.string(), end,
@@ -1075,7 +1140,7 @@ bool ReadRecords(
             file.read(tail.data(), tail.size());
             const u64 records = where[1], facts_at = where[2], facts = where[3];
             const u64 programs_at = where[4], programs = where[5];
-            if (std::memcmp(tail.data(), SetMagic, 8) != 0 || where[0] != 12 || facts_at < 12 ||
+            if (std::memcmp(tail.data(), magic.data(), 8) != 0 || where[0] != 12 || facts_at < 12 ||
                 programs_at < facts_at || programs_at > end - TrailerBytes) {
                 return false;
             }
@@ -1122,7 +1187,7 @@ bool ReadRecords(
             std::scoped_lock lock{set_index_mutex};
             set_index = index;
         }
-        std::vector<char> bytes, fact, code, key;
+        std::vector<char> bytes, fact, code, key, stored;
         std::array<u64, 6> hashes{};
         for (const SetIndex::Record& record : index->records) {
             // 0780: a compute record goes to on_compute only; a reader without one never sees it.
@@ -1157,9 +1222,15 @@ bool ReadRecords(
                 fact.resize(f.size);
                 seek(f.at);
                 file.read(fact.data(), fact.size());
-                code.resize(c.size);
                 seek(c.at);
-                file.read(code.data(), code.size());
+                if (packed) {
+                    stored.resize(c.size);
+                    file.read(stored.data(), stored.size());
+                    if (!UnpackProgram(unpacker.get(), stored, code)) return false;
+                } else {
+                    code.resize(c.size);
+                    file.read(code.data(), code.size());
+                }
                 AppendEnvironment(bytes, fact, code);
             }
             bytes.insert(bytes.end(), key.begin(), key.end());
@@ -1216,21 +1287,26 @@ bool ForEachProgramCode(const std::filesystem::path& path, u32 cache_version,
         // `wanted` is not asked.
         static constexpr char OldMagic[9] = "edenset2";
         const bool old_layout = std::memcmp(magic.data(), OldMagic, 8) == 0;
-        if ((!old_layout && std::memcmp(magic.data(), SetMagic, 8) != 0) ||
+        // 0830: "edenset4", each program's code packed (unpacked before `on_program` sees it).
+        const bool packed = std::memcmp(magic.data(), PackedMagic, 8) == 0;
+        if ((!old_layout && !packed && std::memcmp(magic.data(), SetMagic, 8) != 0) ||
             version != cache_version) {
             return true;
         }
+        std::unique_ptr<ZSTD_DCtx, FreeDContext> unpacker{packed ? ZSTD_createDCtx() : nullptr};
+        if (packed && !unpacker) return false;
         std::array<u64, 6> where{};
         seek(end - TrailerBytes);
         get(where);
         file.read(tail.data(), tail.size());
         const u64 programs_at = where[4], programs = where[5];
-        if (std::memcmp(tail.data(), old_layout ? OldMagic : SetMagic, 8) != 0 || where[0] != 12 ||
+        if (std::memcmp(tail.data(), magic.data(), 8) != 0 || where[0] != 12 ||
             programs_at < where[2] || programs_at > end - TrailerBytes) {
             return false;
         }
         const u64 entry_head = old_layout ? 12 : 20;
         std::vector<u8> code;
+        std::vector<char> stored, unpacked;
         u64 at = programs_at;
         for (u64 i = 0; i < programs; ++i) {
             u32 program{};
@@ -1242,9 +1318,17 @@ bool ForEachProgramCode(const std::filesystem::path& path, u32 cache_version,
             get(size);
             if (size > end - TrailerBytes - (at + entry_head)) return false;
             if (old_layout || wanted(hash)) {
-                code.resize(static_cast<size_t>(size));
-                file.read(reinterpret_cast<char*>(code.data()), static_cast<std::streamsize>(size));
-                on_program(hash, std::span<const u8>{code.data(), code.size()});
+                if (packed) {
+                    stored.resize(static_cast<size_t>(size));
+                    file.read(stored.data(), static_cast<std::streamsize>(size));
+                    if (!UnpackProgram(unpacker.get(), stored, unpacked)) return false;
+                    on_program(hash, std::span<const u8>{reinterpret_cast<const u8*>(unpacked.data()),
+                                                         unpacked.size()});
+                } else {
+                    code.resize(static_cast<size_t>(size));
+                    file.read(reinterpret_cast<char*>(code.data()), static_cast<std::streamsize>(size));
+                    on_program(hash, std::span<const u8>{code.data(), code.size()});
+                }
             }
             at += entry_head + size;
         }
